// `Int.shift_left` written as a call is the `<<<` operator, an Int operation
// lowered as the operator is, so its fault is the operator's text at the
// call's line: `line 9: negative shift count -1`, with no function name in
// it, where `String.repeat`'s reads `strings.String.repeat: …`.
import std/io

fn main() {
    io.print("before")
    io.print("${Int.shift_left(1, 0 - 1)}")
}
